 when communicating. So reliability high, stress resilience high, technical competence good, but communication issues may affect crew cooperation.\n\nCandidate C: can make correct decisions quickly, difficulty communicating ideas, regarded as egocentric, not willing to further education, puts concern for others above everything, excellent attention skills. So decision quality good, attention good, but communication issues, egocentric, not willing to develop. Concern for others is good for cooperation, but egocentric contradictory. Might be mixed.\n\nCandidate D: responds to unexpected events adequately, can concentrate very well, solves problems extremely well, takes responsibility seriously, considered moody, regarded as a loner. So reliability, responsibility, problem solving good, but moody and loner may affect crew cooperation.\n\nWe need to start discussion. Perhaps pick Candidate B as leading due to strong reliability and stress handling, despite communication tone issues. Or Candidate D with responsibility and problem solving but moody. Candidate B seems strongest overall.\n\nThus I will state my current recommendation: Candidate B. Provide evidence: very conscientious (reliability), handles stress well (stress resilience), good at assessing weather (technical competence), but note communication concerns. Argue that strengths outweigh concerns, but we need to discuss others.\n\nLet's produce public message and metadata."}
